reagent-name-propofol = propofol
reagent-desc-propofol = Fast intravenous anesthetic. 3u+ in blood means deep sleep; clears in a couple of minutes. 30u+ depresses breathing.
reagent-name-ketamine = ketamine
reagent-desc-ketamine = Dissociative anesthetic and strong painkiller. Small doses kill pain, 10u+ puts to sleep. 30u+ depresses breathing.
reagent-name-midazolam = midazolam
reagent-desc-midazolam = Long-acting sedative: drowsiness and sluggishness, 15u+ puts to sleep. 40u+ depresses breathing.
