reagent-name-paracetamol = paracetamol
reagent-desc-paracetamol = Mild long-acting painkiller. Safe in normal doses; 25u+ in blood damages the liver.
reagent-name-tramadol = tramadol
reagent-desc-tramadol = Moderate painkiller. Drowsy at 15u, 30u+ depresses breathing. Mildly addictive.
reagent-name-morphine = morphine
reagent-desc-morphine = Strong painkiller: drowsiness, sluggishness. 25u+ depresses breathing. Addictive.
reagent-name-promedol = promedol
reagent-desc-promedol = Strong fast painkiller (military). 20u+ depresses breathing. Highly addictive.
reagent-name-naloxone = naloxone
reagent-desc-naloxone = Opioid antidote: quickly purges morphine, promedol and tramadol. Triggers withdrawal in addicts.
reagent-name-calcitonin = calcitonin
reagent-desc-calcitonin = Speeds bone knitting under a splint; at 5u+ bones slowly knit even without one.
reagent-name-ademetionine = ademetionine
reagent-desc-ademetionine = Restores the liver.
reagent-name-salbutamol = salbutamol
reagent-desc-salbutamol = Restores the lungs and eases breathing.
reagent-name-digoxin = digoxin
reagent-desc-digoxin = Restores the heart. 15u+ damages the heart, 20u+ depresses breathing.
reagent-name-piracetam = piracetam
reagent-desc-piracetam = Restores the brain.
reagent-name-ipidacrine = ipidacrine
reagent-desc-ipidacrine = Gradually repairs damaged nerves.
